Setting pwdLastSet to 0

• What it does: Forces the user to change their password immediately at the next logon.


Setting pwdLastSet to -1

• What it does: Marks the password as "last updated right now" and clears the forced reset block.


Option 2: The Math Approach (Fine-Grained Password Policies)

If you want to target a group of users rather than a single individual, you can use Active Directory's Fine-Grained Password Policies (FGPP) to artificially force an expiration on a specific timeline.
• How it works: You calculate the exact number of days between today and your target target date. You then create a Password Settings Object (PSO), set the Maximum password age to that number of days, and apply it to the user.
• The Catch: This goes strictly by the days elapsed since the user last changed their password. If they change their password tomorrow, the expiration date shifts forward, so it is not a fixed calendar date.


